@title Telemetry Pipeline Architecture
@subtitle Skerry Wind Power, 6 offshore wind farms. Region eu-north-1, reviewed 2026-10-02
@author Asset Data team

# Overview

Turbine readings flow from each farm into one central stream and are processed once. The stream processor then splits them into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

# Pipeline diagram

diagram pipe dir=LR title="Telemetry pipeline"
pipe: tc "Turbine Controllers" ext
pipe: eg "Edge Gateway" ext
pipe: stream "Telemetry Stream" queue
pipe: sp "Stream Processor" svc focus
pipe: ts "Timeseries Store" db
pipe: arch "Raw Archive" store
pipe: alert "Alerting Service" svc
pipe: dash "Operations Dashboard" user
pipe: tc -> eg : OPC UA, 1 Hz
pipe: eg -> stream : MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 s
pipe: stream -> sp : consumer
pipe: sp -> ts : 10 s aggregates
pipe: sp -> arch : Parquet every 15 minutes
pipe: sp -> alert : threshold breach
pipe: ts -> dash : queries
pipe: group site "On site at each farm, outside the cloud account" tc, eg
pipe: group cloud "Cloud account" stream, sp, ts, arch, alert, dash

# Capacity and retention

- **Telemetry Stream:** 24 shards, 18000 messages per second at peak. Retention not recorded.
- **Timeseries Store:** 7 days in memory and 3 years on magnetic storage.
- **Raw Archive:** 10 years, moved to cold storage after 90 days.

# If the uplink fails

The Edge Gateway buffers up to 6 hours of readings on disk and replays them in order when the link returns.

!! The buffer holds 6 hours only. After that the oldest readings are dropped and cannot be replayed.
